cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "multilayer-erdos-renyi: Erdos-Renyi random graphs over a multilayer social network"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: John Edisson
    family-names: Tapias Zarrazola
    affiliation: Universidad de Antioquia
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-06"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kemquiros/Erdos-Renyi-social-Network-prototype"
keywords:
  - Erdos-Renyi
  - random graphs
  - multilayer networks
  - social network analysis
  - Java
abstract: >-
  A generator for Erdos-Renyi G(n, p) random graphs over a multilayer social
  network, where each layer carries its own directedness. Includes degree
  distributions, connected components and the giant-component threshold, all
  asserted against their analytic values in the test suite. Originating as a
  2015 NetBeans prototype at Universidad de Antioquia, it was rebuilt in 2026
  on Java 21 with Maven. The rewrite documents that the original never used its
  Erdos-Renyi parameter: the computed probability underflowed a double to zero
  and was then overwritten with a hardcoded 0.5.
